      en: "The Timbuktu palm groves lie north of the city, along the Niger River banks and in surrounding oases. They consist mainly of date palms cultivated for centuries. Date palms are a vital food and income source for the local population, mainly Tuareg and Songhai. The groves are managed using traditional irrigation techniques. Timbuktu was once a center of trans-Saharan trade, and the palm groves provided food for caravans. Today, they symbolize resilience in the desert region.",
